"""The test that exercises each function of dash_render.py -- and each
function the generated server app defines for itself -- for WP-24's
AC-24.3 and CLAUDE.md rule 4.

Read by test/test_function_test_map.py, which fails when dash_render.py
gains a function this map does not name, when an entry names a test that
does not exist, or when a DEAD or TEST_ONLY function becomes reachable.

Keys are ``co_qualname``s: ``GlyphMapper.map_scatter``, a nested
``_dash_build_hover.<locals>._band``, and ``app:make_document`` for a
function only the app template defines.  A function the app copies from
dash_render.py is the same entry as the original.

How the tests were chosen (WP-24, 24sep2026, at a2c7502): the whole suite
ran under scripts/fncov/ with DASH_FNCOV_PER_TEST=1, recording every
function each test executes, and each function was given the most focused
test that executed it -- one whose own source names it, else the one that
executed the fewest dash functions.  Then every entry was mutation-checked:
the function's body skipped in a scratch copy and the named test run alone
(scripts/fncov/fncov_mutate.py --map).  Where the named test passed anyway
(91 of 467), the entry names instead a test seen to fail when the body is
skipped (fncov_mutate.py over every test that executes the function); where
none did, test_function_audit.py was written and is named.  So every
entry's test failed, when this was written, with its function broken.
Re-derive with fncov_report.py --suggest-map; verify with --check-map and
fncov_mutate.py --map.
"""

